SUMMARY:Neil Frances DJ Set and a Special Guest Featuring Never-Before-Seen Technology *sold out!*
DESCRIPTION:Thursday July 16th\, 2026\nThis event is sold out!\nDoors | 7:00 PM\nShow | 8:00 PM \nGeneral Admission Standing Room | $10 + Fees \nPlease note this event is 21+ – Valid ID Required to Drink\nCome hungry! Snacks and light bites will be available at the canteen.\nFeaturing food truck – Big Back Burger! Grab delish burgers & more located right outside the main entrance.\n————————————————–\nNeil Frances DJ Set and a Special Guest featuring Never-Before-Seen Technology!  \n*Free drink to first 500 in the door* \nDemocratizing Dance Music | Portion of Proceeds to benefit Femme House \nLA duo NEIL FRANCES is the brainchild of Australian Jordan Feller and Californian Marc Gilfry. Starting as a production duo\, their demos were accidentally discovered by tastemakers like KCRW & triple j\, forcing them into the spotlight. Dance-floor sociologists from the start\, the pair organized a live band with bassist Greg Cham & drummer Rhythm Luna. They have sold out tours\, opened for acts like Jungle\, Odesza\, & Unknown Mortal Orchestra\, and evolved into a festival staple playing over 20 renowned festivals\, including Lollapalooza & ACL. In 2024\, they are confirmed for Coachella\, Electric Forest & Bonnaroo. \nFeller\, an old-school hip-hop head and rave kid\, has a gift for sonic recall and beats-based production\, while singer/guitarist Gilfry writes melodies and hooks on command. The result is genre-spanning club-ready grooves with influences ranging from rave culture\, funk & soul\, yacht rock\, & hip-hop. You will just as likely hear a sample flip as you will a guitar run through a tape machine. \nTheir 2018 EP Took A While showcased their infectious sound to critical acclaim. Global attention followed when their cover of Stardust’s “Music Sounds Better With You” went viral\, earning Gold Certification. In 2022\, they released their debut LP There Is No Neil Frances\, a concept album centered on manifestation and self-realization. It’s All a Bit Fuzzy followed in 2023\, showcasing their love for collaborations with rising talent like dreamcastmoe\, St. Panther\, PawPaw Rod\, & DRAMA. \nSupported by: DJ Major Vibes\nMajor Vibes is an established DJ\, event producer\, and musical tastemaker shaping the nightlife landscape of Lancaster\, Pennsylvania. With a genre-fluid approach rooted in disco\, funk\, house\, and global dance music\, he delivers high-energy performances built on thoughtful curation and technical skill. His events consistently draw diverse\, engaged audiences\, making him a go-to choice for venues\, festivals\, and brand collaborations seeking intentional artistry and unforgettable experiences.\n————————————————–\nPLEASE NOTE:\nThis event will be a phone-free experience.\nUse of cellphones\, cameras\, or recording devices will not be permitted in the performance space. \nUpon arrival at the venue\, all phones will be secured in Yondr pouches that will be opened at the end of the event. Guests maintain possession of their belongings at all times and can access their phones throughout the event at designated Phone Use Areas. All phones will be re-secured in Yondr pouches before returning to the event space. \nAnyone seen using a non-permitted device during the performance will be escorted out of the venue. Guests are encouraged to bring a credit card for purchases inside the venue. We appreciate your cooperation in creating a phone-free viewing experience.\n————————————————–\n*Ticket Alert* \nTickets for Mickey’s Black Box are sold through TicketMaster\, via our website\, or in person at our Box Office. Any tickets purchased elsewhere will not be honored and we are not responsible for tickets purchased from any 3rd party sellers. Do not google the name of the band to search for tickets. Go to Mickeysblackbox.com ONLY. Mickeysblackbox.com will never direct you anywhere but the official TicketMaster event site. \n\nAll bags are subject are to search upon entry. Tickets are non-refundable\, save for instances in which performances are cancelled by Mickey’s Black Box. For more information about our venue or to make an ADA request\, please visit the FAQ page of our website: https://mickeysblackbox.com/faq/ or call our box office line at (717) 723 – 8463.
URL:https://mickeysblackbox.com/event/neil-frances-and-a-special-guest-featuring-never-before-seen-technology/
LOCATION:Mickey’s Black Box\, 101 Rock Lititz Boulevard\, Lititz\, PA\, 17543\, United States
