SUMMARY:Local Art Live!
DESCRIPTION:Friday July 24th\, 2026\nDoors | 6:30 PM\nShow | 7:30 PM \nEvent Ticket | $19.50 + Fees \n+$2 on All Day of Show Purchases\nThis event is all ages – 21+ With Valid ID Required to Drink\nCome hungry! Snacks and light bites will be available at the canteen.\n—————————————————\nPresented by Mickey’s Black Box\n—————————————————\nCome out and enjoy a great night of live music\, artistic expression\, and delicious drinks – highlighting the incredible talent in our backyard! \nFeaturing Bands – Lysdexia\, Coal\, & Burn The Martyr \nLysdexia\nCentral PA based Metal Prog Band featuring – Dave-vocals\, Jake-vocals/guitars\, Matt-guitars\, Jason-bass\, and Joe-drums \nCoal\nCoal\, one of Central Pennsylvania’s electrifying live alternative rock bands. Twice Nominated Central Pennsylvania’s Best Hard Rock Band the band consistently writes and releases music tough to ignore. Representing a diverse\, stead fast and powerful face of modern rock featuring singer Dal Dawn\, drummer Josh Freeburn\, and bassist Liam Daizey keep moving forward in spite of all the changes around them.  \nThe band has toured the Mid-Atlantic alongside friends and fello musicians Any Given Sin\, Awake at Last\, and Rise Among Rivals and many others. They also have had the honor of sharing the stage with National greats such as Halestorm\,  Hinder\, Tantric\, Saving Abel\, and more. They remain committed to keeping our sound fresh\, active\, and alive and continue to work on new releases keeping themselves fresh and alive for every new listener.  \nBurn The Martyr\nHailing from York\, Pennsylvania\, Burn the Martyr is a hard-hitting rock/metal band known for blending raw intensity with melodic edge. Drawing influence from modern hard rock and classic metal roots\, the band delivers a sound that is both aggressive and emotionally driven\, built on heavy riffs\, powerful vocals\, and tight\, high-energy performances. \nSince emerging on the regional scene\, Burn the Martyr has built a reputation for commanding live shows and a no-frills\, authentic approach to their music. Their songs explore themes of struggle\, resilience\, and personal transformation\, resonating with audiences who connect with honest\, hard-edged storytelling. With a stage presence that balances grit and precision\, they bring a full-throttle experience to every performance — whether in intimate venues or larger festival settings. \nCommitted to evolving their sound while staying true to their heavy roots\, Burn the Martyr continues to carve out their place in the Pennsylvania rock scene\, pushing forward with new material\, relentless drive\, and a passion for music that hits as hard as it feels. \nBurn the Martyr is: Corey Burnard – Vocals/Rhythm Guitar Mark Koncki – Drums Tim Risser – Bass Guitar Tyler Acton – Lead Guitar \nFeaturing Local Vendors – Chele Creates\, Rory Lamoreaux\, Issac Westlund\, Bouncing Goat Soap Co\, & Lawler Creative!\n—————————————————\n*Ticket Alert*  \nTickets for Mickey’s Black Box are sold through TicketMaster\, via our website\, or in person at our Box Office. Any tickets purchased elsewhere will not be honored and we are not responsible for tickets purchased from any 3rd party sellers.  Do not google the name of the band to search for tickets.  Go to Mickeysblackbox.com ONLY. Mickeysblackbox.com will never direct you anywhere but the official TicketMaster event site. \n\nAll bags are subject are to search upon entry. Tickets are non-refundable\, save for instances in which performances are cancelled by Mickey’s Black Box. For more information about our venue or to make an ADA request\, please visit the FAQ page of our website: https://mickeysblackbox.com/faq/ or call our box office line at (717) 723 – 8463.
URL:https://mickeysblackbox.com/event/local-art-live-3/
LOCATION:Mickey’s Black Box\, 101 Rock Lititz Boulevard\, Lititz\, PA\, 17543\, United States
